STATEMENT_RESULT NextStateARM8_erase hyps 0 concl_literal true
STATEMENT Next_erase (E1-0003 text; NOT derived here: no SP premise) typechecks true free_vars [s::arm8_state]
s.PSTATE.EL = 0w ∧ s.exception = NoException ∧
(Next s).exception = NoException ∧ untagged (Next (erase s)).PC ⇒
Next (erase s) = erase (Next s)
STATEMENT_CHANGE Next_erase_sp = E1-0003 Next_erase plus the SP premise (~s.SCTLR_EL1.SA0 \/ aligned 4 s.SP_EL0)
OLD_TEXT (E1-0003 Next_erase): s.PSTATE.EL = 0w /\ s.exception = NoException /\ (arm8$Next s).exception = NoException /\ untagged (arm8$Next (erase s)).PC ==> arm8$Next (erase s) = erase (arm8$Next s)
NEW_TEXT (Next_erase_sp): s.PSTATE.EL = 0w /\ s.exception = NoException /\ (~s.SCTLR_EL1.SA0 \/ aligned 4 s.SP_EL0) /\ (arm8$Next s).exception = NoException /\ untagged (arm8$Next (erase s)).PC ==> arm8$Next (erase s) = erase (arm8$Next s)
WHY: without the premise the equation is false when SA0 and ~aligned 4 SP_EL0 at an SP-based access (E1-0003 N2: the real state faults, the erased one does not)
STATEMENT Next_erase_sp typechecks true free_vars [s::arm8_state]
s.PSTATE.EL = 0w ∧ s.exception = NoException ∧
(¬s.SCTLR_EL1.SA0 ∨ aligned 4 s.SP_EL0) ∧ (Next s).exception = NoException ∧
untagged (Next (erase s)).PC ⇒
Next (erase s) = erase (Next s)
